; pwball_pal_accumulate: Composes the palette by ACCUMULATION: it walks wf_pal_delta and ADDS each
;   increment to the buffer's colour, wf_pal_count colours, and takes one step off wf_pal_steps. It
;   is the fade, and it is the reason each colour takes SIX bytes: they are words, so they can
;   accumulate without clipping, and the upload keeps the low byte. Located with a write watchpoint
;   on the buffer, not by reading the disassembly
